# Accessibility

## Keyboard navigation

Keyboard drag-and-drop is powered by `KeyboardSensor` and is active by default. Focusable items have `role="button"` and `tabindex="0"` automatically set.

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `Tab` | Move focus between draggable items |
| `Enter` / `Space` | Pick up the focused item and start drag |
| `ArrowDown` / `ArrowRight` | Move preview to next position |
| `ArrowUp` / `ArrowLeft` | Move preview to previous position |
| `Enter` | Drop at current preview position |
| `Escape` | Cancel drag, ghost returns to origin |

Arrow keys navigate both within and across containers. When the end of a container is reached, focus jumps to the first position of the next container (and vice-versa at the start).

## Screen-reader announcements

`DndProvider` renders a visually-hidden ARIA live region (`aria-live="assertive"`) that announces drag events to screen readers. The default announcements are:

| Event | Default message |
|-------|----------------|
| Drag start | `"Picked up item."` |
| Drag over new position | `"Moving to position {n} of {total}."` |
| Drop | `"Dropped item."` |
| Cancel | `"Drop cancelled."` |

### Custom announcements

Pass `announcements` in the `DndController` constructor to customise the messages:

```ts
import { DndController, defaultAnnouncements } from '@horuse/svelte-dnd';

const controller = new DndController({
    announcements: {
        ...defaultAnnouncements,
        onDragStart: () => 'Picked up a task. Use arrow keys to move it.',
        onDragOver: (containerId, position, total) =>
            `Moving to column ${containerId}, position ${position + 1} of ${total}.`,
        onDrop: () => 'Task placed.',
        onCancel: () => 'Move cancelled, task returned to original position.',
    },
});
```

### Announcements type

```ts
interface Announcements {
    onDragStart: () => string;
    onDragOver: (containerId: string, position: number, total: number) => string;
    onDrop: () => string;
    onCancel: () => string;
}
```

## ARIA attributes

The library sets these attributes automatically:

| Element | Attributes |
|---------|-----------|
| `DndDraggable` inner div | `role="button"`, `tabindex="0"`, `aria-grabbed`, `aria-roledescription="draggable item"` |
| `DndDroppable` | `aria-disabled` when `disabled={true}` |

## use:draggable action

The `draggable` action sets the same ARIA attributes on any element, without requiring `DndDraggable`:

```svelte
<li
    use:draggable={{ id: item.id, controller }}
    style="transform: translate3d({controller.translations.get(item.id)?.x ?? 0}px, {controller.translations.get(item.id)?.y ?? 0}px, 0)"
>
    {item.label}
</li>
```

The `use:draggable` action also adds/removes the CSS class `dnd-dragging` during a drag, so you can style it without Svelte reactivity.

